    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this superb one-bedroom apartment to the Dublin city centre property market. Ideally positioned on Usher's Quay in the heart of Dublin 8, No. 5 Traders Wharf offers c. 44 sqm of well-proportioned, light-filled accommodation, presenting a phenomenal opportunity for first-time buyers, city professionals, or savvy investors seeking an exceptionally secure, low-maintenance home in an unbeatable central location.\nThe location is second to none. Situated right along the Quays in central Dublin, Traders Wharf puts you within comfortable walking distance of Smithfield, Temple Bar, Christchurch, Trinity College, and the central shopping districts of Grafton Street and Henry Street. The surrounding neighbourhood is vibrant and bustling, packed with artisan cafes, award-winning restaurants, local bars, and cultural landmarks like the Guinness Storehouse and IMMA. Transport options are unrivalled, with the Luas Red Line at Smithfield and Four Courts just across the river, Heuston Station nearby, and numerous prime bus corridors passing right outside your front door.\nInternal living accommodation of c. 44 sqm is smartly laid out to make optimal use of every square meter. Upon entering, a welcoming hallway leads to a generous double bedroom complete with built-in wardrobes, a sleek tiled main bathroom suite, a separate fully fitted kitchen, and a bright, expansive living room area. A standout feature of No. 5 is the private, west-facing Jack and Jill balcony, offering a quiet, sun-filled outdoor retreat capturing afternoon and evening light. Positioned within a mature, well-managed, and secure development, the property offers quiet privacy right in the centre of the action and benefits from its own designated car space.\nProperties in Traders Wharf are consistently in high demand due to their prime positioning and strong city-centre appeal. Viewing is highly advised, call RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS today for further information or to arrange a viewing!\nAdditional Features;\n•c. 44 sqm\n•BER D\n•Mngt fees c. 2,199 per annum \n•1 BED / 1 BATH\n•Private west-facing Jack and Jill balcony capturing evening light\n•Prime Dublin 8 city centre location on Usher's Quay\n•Separate fully fitted kitchen\n•Generous double bedroom with fitted built-in wardrobes\n•Sleek, fully tiled main bathroom suite\n•Bright and spacious interior layout\n•Secure, well-maintained development\n•Secure designated parking \n•Minutes on foot to Smithfield, Christchurch, Temple Bar & Grafton Street\n•Short walk to Luas Red Line & Heuston Station\n•Major bus corridors right on your doorstep\n•Ideal for First-Time Buyers, City Professionals, and Investors alike\nDirections\nTraveling inbound along Usher's Quay towards Dublin City Centre, proceed past the junction at Bridge Street (O'Donovan Rossa Bridge). Traders Wharf will be located on your right-hand side along the quayside.\n\n"
      },
